---
layout: null
permalink: /newsletter.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  What the newsletter function announces: every post on the site, newest first.
  All of them, not only the newest, because posts restored from the web archive keep
  their old date. A post with "newsletter: false" in its front matter is never mailed.
  Pictures come through the Netlify Image CDN as JPEG (Outlook can't show WebP),
  cropped to 3:2 from the top so heads in class photos stay in.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign mailposts = site.posts | where_exp: "p", "p.newsletter != false" -%}
{
  "posts": [
    {%- for p in mailposts %}
    {%- capture img %}{% if p.image %}{{ site.url }}/.netlify/images?url={{ p.image | url_encode | replace: "+", "%20" }}&w=1040&h=694&fit=cover&position=top&fm=jpg&q=80{% endif %}{% endcapture %}
    {"title": {{ p.title | jsonify }}, "description": {{ p.description | default: p.excerpt | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip | truncate: 220 | jsonify }}, "url": {{ p.url | absolute_url | jsonify }}, "date": {{ p.date | date_to_xmlschema | jsonify }}, "image": {{ img | strip | jsonify }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
